    web_style_cascade_apply_decls_reparses_per_node_2026-09-12, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: the filed defect is already fixed at this base - commit 0a9150ea6d7 (perf(ui): cut the web cold document pipeline 57% with four exact memos) is an ancestor of HEAD. Proven empirically: probe with 180 .item nodes sharing ONE declaration block under 12 parents (whole-style memo cannot absorb): decl_table_build hits=11 misses=13 - exactly 1 parse of the shared block, 11 cross-group first-applies served from cache; field parity 0 mismatches; per-group em widths correct (65 vs 120px) because the cache stores the parsed table, not computed style. Memo at simple_web_html_layout_renderer_foundation.spl:2427-2457 (bounded DECL_TABLE_MEMO_LIMIT=4096; parse is pure function of text so no staleness). The doc's 86% attribution was mostly mis-attributed per doc/10_metrics/ui/web_style_cascade_after_memo_macos_2026-09-12.md. No src change needed; added the missing cascade-level pin test/01_unit/browser_engine/web_style_cascade_decl_parse_once_spec.spl 4/4 PASS; neighbours style_cascade_memo 6/6, padding_units 8/8, cold_pipeline_memo 4/4, overflow_triple_memo 2/2, linear_scaling 3/3 PASS. Pre-existing decl_apply/declarations coverage-closure failures (url() tokenizer doctests) are unrelated and concurrent-lane-adjacent. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/browser_engine/web_style_cascade_decl_parse_once_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/browser_engine/style_cascade_memo_spec.spl"

